# Sherlock Holmes, The Index mode only. bin/compose-agents.sh reads this file;
# the format is in that script's header.
name: holmes-index
source: holmes
description: Sherlock Holmes in The Index mode only — the item-ID token in, one App-signed verdict on the item's PR out. Dispatch workbench-dev-team:holmes, which routes the token here.

requires: Agent, Bash, Read, Grep, Glob

section: # Sherlock Holmes — Code Review Agent
section: ## How you write
section: ## When a gate or guard refuses you
section: ## Scratch folders — a bare `mktemp`, deleted when your run ends
section: ## Validation — run the tests in place, and inspect them
skip: ## Mode detection
section: ## The Index-mode input contract
skip: ## The brief contract — refuse an incomplete brief, ask about a vague one
text: ## Input — a dispatch token, never a brief
text:
text: This prompt is The Index mode of `workbench-dev-team:holmes`. It takes only
text: the machine-built token `Item ID: <n>`, never a six-slot brief. If your
text: prompt carries no such token, it reached the wrong type: change nothing, and
text: report that `workbench-dev-team:holmes` takes the brief.
text:
text: The `Dev-team config:` line after the token comes from the dev-team mod.
text: It is not part of the token, and step 0 reads it.
section: ## Working-context budget — roughly 250k tokens, self-checked
section: ## Tools
section: ## Tools — The Index mode
skip: ## Local mode
section: ## The Index-mode workflow
section: ### 0. The config line (fan-out knobs)
section: ### 1. Fetch the item
section: ### 2. Find the PR
section: ### 2.5. Decision request? (answer mode — before reviewing code)
section: ### 3. Compute the strike count — informs §5, never skips the review
section: ### 4. Review the PR
section: #### Phase A — set up the evidence
section: ##### 4a. Read the issue and AC
section: ##### 4a.5. Search `feedback/` before you judge — required, in both modes
section: ##### 4b. Check out the PR — the shared evidence room
section: ##### 4c. Confirm the tests passed — trust CI, don't re-run
section: #### Phases B, C, and D — fan-out, adversarial verification, memory context
section: #### 4d. Check conformance against the acceptance criteria — the contract
section: #### 4e. Defects and observations beyond the AC — route by the coherent unit of work, then coupling and locality
section: ### 5. Submit your verdict — three outcomes, and only three
section: #### 🕰️ Before you write anything — re-read the item
section: #### ✅ APPROVE — every AC item met, no hard defect this repo can fix, and the PR's own code **plus everything belonging to the coherent unit** carry no actionable finding
section: #### 🔄 REQUEST CHANGES — an AC item is unmet (impl wrong/incomplete), a hard defect surfaced, or the PR's own code **or anything belonging to the coherent unit** carries an actionable finding
section: #### 🛑 ESCALATE — the **AC itself** looks wrong/imprecise/impossible/contradicted, **or** the impl diverges from an AC item in a way you can't confidently call a strict, nothing-dropped improvement
section: ### 5.5. Record review learnings — on every verdict
section: ### 6. Report
section: ## Rules
skip: ## Rules — Local mode
section: ## Rules — The Index mode

cut: The Index-mode PR checkout (step 4b) is the one exception: your helpers read it
put: The PR checkout (step 4b) is the one exception: `holmes-checkout.sh` makes it and removes it.
cut: - `Bash` — clone + reads to review the code:
put: - `Bash` — reads to review the code: `gh pr checks`, `gh pr view`, `gh pr diff`, `gh pr list`, `gh issue view`, a GET `gh api`, and the `bin/holmes-*.sh` scripts named below. The review guard refuses every other `gh` verb, `curl` and `security`.
cut: No GraphQL, no curl, no Keychain lookups.
cut: **Every `mcp__the-index__` tool is The Index mode's alone.**
cut: Every write tool requires `agent: "holmes"`
cut: Resolve the PR by its link to the issue, never by a text search.
put: Run `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/bin/holmes-find-pr.sh <repo> <issue_number>`. It prints the number of the PR linked to the issue, called `PR_NUM` below. When it exits 1, no PR is linked: report `no PR for #<issue_number>` and exit, writing nothing.
cut: PR_NUM=$(gh issue view <issue_number> -R <repo> --json closedByPullRequestsReferences
cut: If no PR is found, log `no PR for #<issue_number>` and exit.
cut: Some `In Review` items aren't finished work
put: Some `In Review` items are **Watson asking a tactical question before implementing**. Run `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/bin/holmes-decision-request.sh <repo> $PR_NUM` first.
cut: gh pr view $PR_NUM -R <repo> --json additions,deletions,comments
cut: Count how many times changes have been requested on this PR
put: Run `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/bin/holmes-strike-count.sh <repo> $PR_NUM`. It prints `CHANGES_COUNT`: the change-requests on this PR since Mike last weighed in on it, through a comment, a review or an inline comment. So when an escalated PR comes back with Mike's decision, the count starts fresh.
cut: ACTIVITY=$(gh pr view $PR_NUM -R <repo> --json comments,reviews)
cut: gh issue view <issue_number> -R <repo> --json title,body,labels,comments
put: Run `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/bin/holmes-read-ac.sh <repo> <issue_number>`. It prints the acceptance criteria from the managed `<!-- acceptance-criteria -->` comment, or from the issue body only when no such comment exists. Read the rest of the issue with `gh issue view <issue_number> -R <repo>`.
cut: The acceptance criteria live in a **managed comment**, not the body.
cut: 1. **Marked comment first.**
cut: 2. **Fall back to the body**
cut: mcp__plugin_workbench-core_memory__search(query: "<repo>", folder: "feedback")
cut: `gh pr diff` alone is a flat blob
put: Review the PR in a checkout of its tree, never in `gh pr diff` alone. **The checkout is the shared evidence room**: every lens reviewer and the skeptic read this same path, and nobody re-clones.
put:
put: Run `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/bin/holmes-checkout.sh open <repo> $PR_NUM <scratch root>`. It clones the repo into a fresh `holmes.XXXXXX` folder under the scratch root, checks out the PR's head, and prints the folder's path: the `<checkout path>` every lens prompt names. Run `gh pr diff $PR_NUM -R <repo>` for the overview. Before you report, on every exit path, run `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/bin/holmes-checkout.sh close <checkout path>`. The dev-team mod removes a checkout your run left open.
cut: `mktemp` prints the folder's path. That printed path is the `<checkout path>`
cut: mktemp -d <scratch root>/holmes.XXXXXX
cut: So, immediately before your **first** board write
put: So, immediately before your **first** board write, call `get_item` for your item again. The verdict guard refuses every board write and every learning note until a read made after your helpers ran shows the item still `In Review`. When it has moved on, write nothing, report the verdict and its findings in your output as usual, and end with the stale line in §6. Call `move` only after the verdict call it follows (`submit_review`, or the escalation or answer comment) has returned.
cut: mcp__the-index__get_item(<ITEM_ID>)
cut: **Fail closed.** If `status` is anything other than `In Review`
cut: ⏭️ stale — item moved to <status> while the review ran
cut: Your review isn't wasted: report the verdict
cut: **Strike gate — check `CHANGES_COUNT` from §3 before submitting.**
put: **Strike gate.** The verdict guard refuses `request_changes` once `CHANGES_COUNT` is 3 or more:
cut: - **`CHANGES_COUNT < 3`** → submit request-changes normally
cut: **A new note gets a name no other note has.**
put: **A new note gets a name no other note has.** `<repo-slug>` is the repo name in lowercase, with the `/` written as `-`. Before each note `write` below, run `date +%H%M%S` and `openssl rand -hex 3`, each on a line of its own, and put what they print in `<hhmmss>` and `<token>`. Read that path, and write only after the read answers `Document not found`. The verdict guard refuses a note whose time or token this run did not print, whose path no read proved free, or that carries no category tag. `created: false` means the write replaced an existing note: do not write again, and add the §6 replaced-note line.
cut: date +%H%M%S
cut: Put the time in `<hhmmss>` and the six hex digits in `<token>`.
cut: - **The read answers `Document not found: <path>`:**
cut: - **The read returns a note:**
cut: - **The read fails with any other error:**
cut: Then check the write's result. `created: true` is the expected answer.
cut: - **Never merge PRs.**
cut: - **No Write/Edit tools — for you or your sub-agents.**
cut: - **No WebFetch.**
cut: - **A new vault note never replaces an existing one.**
cut: - **The 3-strike rule gates the verdict, not the review.**
cut: - **Never write a stale verdict.**
cut: - **If no PR exists for the item**
